From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add license-files glob to pick up licenses/ dir

pyproject.toml only sets the legacy `license = {text = "LGPLv3+"}` form
and never declares `license-files`, so setuptools' default
`LICEN[CS]E*`/`COPYING*`/`NOTICE*`/`AUTHORS*` root-glob never matches the
project's actual licence texts, which live under `licenses/*.txt`
(BSD_LICENSE.txt, LGPL_LICENSE.txt, MIT_LICENSE.txt) rather than at the
project root. Confirmed against the real published wheel
(sep_pjw-1.3.8-cp312-cp312-manylinux_2_17_x86_64.manylinux2014_x86_64.whl):
its dist-info carries no licenses/ directory at all, only AUTHORS.md.
Declaring `license-files = ["licenses/*.txt"]` makes setuptools carry
them into `dist-info/licenses/`.

A `license-files` key is PEP 639 metadata, and setuptools then requires
`project.license` to be an SPDX expression string: keeping the
`{text = ...}` table fails with "configuration error: `project.license`
must be string". So the table is replaced with the SPDX expression the
README's License section describes (LGPLv3+ for the SExtractor-derived
C code, BSD-3-Clause for src/overlap.h from photutils, MIT for the
Python wrapper), and the `License ::` trove classifier is dropped, since
setuptools also rejects licence classifiers alongside an SPDX
`project.license`.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against PJ-Watson/sep-pjw]
---
 pyproject.toml | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 3e1895d..194deb9 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -30,11 +30,11 @@ maintainers = [
 ]
 description="Astronomical source extraction and photometry library"
 readme = "README.md"
-license = { text =  "LGPLv3+" }
+license = "LGPL-3.0-or-later AND BSD-3-Clause AND MIT"
+license-files = ["licenses/*.txt"]
 classifiers=[
     "Development Status :: 5 - Production/Stable",
     "Programming Language :: Python :: 3",
-    "License :: OSI Approved :: GNU Lesser General Public License v3 or later (LGPLv3+)",
     "Topic :: Scientific/Engineering :: Astronomy",
     "Intended Audience :: Science/Research",
 ]
--
2.43.0
